WEBVTT

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.920
What...

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.130
What is this...?

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.460
Live, live on, with all your might

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.920
Follow the light to the future

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:45.790
Betrayed and left behind in this lonely world

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:51.330
Fearing a tomorrow I've lost sight of

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.460
I search for the place I belong

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:00.960
My heart screams out, "I want to be needed"

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:09.750
I want to puzzle out these entwined identities, but can I trust them?

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.130
Live, live on, with all your might

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:17.130
Follow the light to the future

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.630
Even if you lose everything

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:24.960
Stay connected to hope

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:28.670
I don't know why I'm here

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.540
But that's all right with me right now

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.420
I have to overcome and press on

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:42.330
So I can smile with you again

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:58.830
<b>A Good Warrior Isn't Always A Good Boss</b>

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.000
That's just the problem!

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.710
My father always assumes everyone is on his level!

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:03.670
Yeah, I totally get that,
and why this has got you so angry, Julietta.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.500
Let's calm down a bit and have some tea.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.670
It's from Raudadola.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.000
My apologies.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:14.830
So to summarize what
you've heard from General Edvard...

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.540
"Oh, no, the soldiers I put through
a hellish training regimen..."

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.170
"...were defeated by a mere arch chimera!"

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:28.790
What a pathetic lot! Weaklings, all of you!

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:33.420
The responsibility for this failure lies
in the man who trained them: myself alone!

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:40.170
And the only way to atone for it is by taking my own life!

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.750
Talk about a Grade-A moron.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.000
Not like dying would...

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:48.580
Lord Leo?

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.670
Oh, sorry.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.830
It's not like dying would make his troops any stronger,
nor would it solve the problem.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:03:00.500
Yes, and thankfully, my father has abandoned
the notion of suicide for now...

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.210
Arch chimeras are among the strongest chimeras.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.920
The men we hired after
the last battle are mere foot soldiers.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:13.290
They had little hope of defeating it with
their lack of experience and training.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:14.790
Right.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.830
I don't know if this is just Edvard,

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.790
but is there a reason he made his newbies fight that?

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:26.830
My father expects everyone to be just as strong as he is.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.130
Oh...

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.670
You understand, yes?

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.630
When my father sees his new soldiers
are unable to defeat an arch chimera,

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:36.580
he thinks his soldiers simply aren't trying hard enough.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.460
Not trying hard enough...

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.130
That's an obnoxious phrase.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.830
And most of the time, it's being
said by the skilled or powerful.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:50.500
They say they have their position
by virtue of their own efforts,

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.170
but that's hardly ever the case.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:57.880
A powerful fighter might've been born
with a more muscular frame.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:02.790
An intelligent planner might've been put
through a good school from an early age.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:07.670
They discount all the external factors
that played a part in their success.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:11.380
Why doesn't my father understand?

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.130
His strength is a boon, yes,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.130
but sadly, it's hard for people to realize
how unique and gifted they are.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:22.540
Because it came naturally to them,
they expect it to come naturally to everyone else.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.830
That's how they delude themselves.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.040
You're right.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:30.210
It's easy for guys like him to assume
everyone's on his level.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.210
The issue we're seeing here is that good warriors do
not always make good teachers.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:38.790
When people want to train others
to be strong like them, what do they do?

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:42.710
They ask themselves what they did to get where they are,

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.920
then have their trainees do just that.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:50.500
If it's too tough for them, a good trainer will make
it easier or change things up,

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.380
but the skilled and powerful can't do that.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:05:00.460
They think the reason their trainees fail is
because they're not trying hard enough.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:56.250
<b>You're fired!</b>

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.830
And Edvard's a real hard worker.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:08.540
That might be part of why he assumes it's effort.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.580
Yes, and after he fought you, Lord Leo...

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.710
Ah, forgive me, should I call you Lord Onyx?

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.250
It's fine, no one's here. Go on.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.670
After he fought you, Lord Leo,
he cursed his lack of training...

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.830
...and redoubled his daily efforts.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:34.330
This probably sounds obvious,
but you really respect him, don't you?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:35.630
I do.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:40.130
I've always wanted to be just like him,
ever since I was little.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:42.750
Sadly...

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:45.750
His stoic, stubborn nature is working against him now,

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:50.420
and his hellish training is making his troops pass out
from exhaustion right on the spot.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.790
I'm surprised they're not just running away screaming.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.710
His soldiers are just as serious about the cause as he is...

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:01.630
So they push themselves to
their limits just to follow his orders.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:05.290
Lord Leo, what should I do?

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.000
Leave it to me.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.670
I'll handle it.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:11.750
Lord Leo!

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:17.670
He's a living weapon created
to defeat demons? Is that true?

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:21.040
I can't say, but that's what he told me.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:26.380
At the very least, I know he lied when
he said he joined us to destroy humanity.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.170
Then why did he join us?

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:35.000
If he wanted to destroy the demon army,
then he needn't take such a roundabout method...

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:39.630
He told me he's going to help us,
though I don't know why.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.170
It's simple!

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.000
He sees we're in trouble and wants to help!

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.000
I don't think that's why...

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.750
He wants to help 'cause he's a good person! I can tell!

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:53.710
Talk about naïve.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:56.130
What?! But he is!

00:06:56.380 --> 00:07:01.000
I will admit, he HAS helped every single one of us here.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:06.460
And of course, if he does anything suspicious,
we'll report him to Queen Echidna.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:12.880
For now, shall we put our trust in him
and keep a close eye on his actions?

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.080
I like that!

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.420
I suppose.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:21.540
I said I'd handle it... But how?

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:24.880
Talking it out with him won't have much of an effect.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:27.960
There's got to be a more direct method...

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.630
You know, there was that thing in Lily's report...

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.710
It's big, it's white, and it's super strong!

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:35.830
That's it!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:42.080
Lord Onyx, are you here?
The Demon Queen is summoning you.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.000
H... He quit?!

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.710
Is that true, Your Highness?

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:51.290
Yes, General Edvard told me himself.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:55.170
He declared he was no longer fit
to lead troops as a general.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.790
So, then, he's left the army?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.210
Actually, no.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:04.960
He's apparently returned to being a common foot soldier
to train with his underlings.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:12.710
Come, my superiors! Let us hunt and defeat
powerful beasts to train ourselves!

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.420
Forward!

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.170
That hasn't solved anything!
That's only made the problem WORSE!

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:24.330
I told him to rethink his decision,
but he refuses to back down on this...

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:28.380
What do you think of this? Have you any--

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.670
Oh, no, my apologies!

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.420
I mustn't rely on you so, it's unbecoming of me!

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.630
I will find a solution myself!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:41.000
Forgive me, Your Highness,
but might I make a proposal?

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:45.290
Would you allow me to handle this situation
involving General Edvard?

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.290
I-I couldn't...

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.000
I will see this resolved.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.710
Very well. I leave it in your hands.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:57.750
At once! I have some preparations to make,
so I will take my leave.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.210
One more thing, Onyx.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:04.880
When this situation is resolved,
there's something I must discuss with you.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.040
Of course, Your Highness.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.750
Here it is, Leo!

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:18.210
This is what Leo was telling me about...

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:22.210
Yes. An artifact from the Machine Age,

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.290
far more powerful than an S-rank chimera.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:28.080
A machine golem!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:29.380
A machine golem...

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:35.420
And this is one from the late end of
the Machine Age, codename Phantom Nine.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:40.750
They were built specifically
to combat high-ranking demons.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.130
And we're going to make use of it...

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:52.130
I've gathered you here not for a training exercise,
but to make an announcement.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.380
As of today,

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.540
I am stepping down from my position
as General and rejoining as a foot soldier.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:05.380
Julietta will be assuming the role of General henceforth.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.290
Oh, Edvard, my sweet, summer child!

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:15.330
This harsh world of ours would
never let you quit that easily.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.750
I'll teach you that lesson here and now.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.290
What is that?

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:47.830
Intruding upon our encampment
and brandishing your weapons at us?

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.710
What are you standing around for?!
Launch a counterattack!

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.330
I am still your general for today! Obey my orders!

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:56.170
Yes, sir!

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:10.580
Don't get too close, now.
You guys shouldn't be fighting this thing.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:15.830
What're you doing?! Retreating from the enemy?
And you call yourselves soldiers?!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.540
I-I'm sorry, sir, but our weapons can't do anything!

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:22.830
If you can't strike it, then draw its attention, or confuse it!

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:25.250
If you've time to complain, you've time to fight!

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:34.170
What's wrong? It stopped.

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:38.830
Oh no, did all that time underground
break its components?

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:41.500
If it doesn't work, then my plans'll be for nothing!

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.080
Crap, is that...

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:46.500
Reflection Ray!

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:52.000
Th-that was close!

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.250
What kind of firepower is this thing packing?!

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:56.460
It melted its own armor...

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.790
The damn thing's safety restrictions are all out of whack!

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:03.580
But I'm a Hero, and I'm going
to make sure no one gets hurt!

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:06.500
What IS that?

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:12.630
We must retreat! It's too powerful!
We can't defeat that! We'll be DEAD!

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.580
It's way more powerful than I expected.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:16.710
What do I do?

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.420
I brought this out for Edvard to fight,

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:21.580
but should I take care of it instead?

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:26.460
The big doll wants to play, does it?

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:28.130
I'll smash it to pieces!

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.000
Stop, you moron! Get down!

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:35.670
What in the...

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.250
That's an ancient laser weapon!

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:42.580
It'll sear right through your dragon scales!

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:43.580
Lord Leo?!

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.540
Listen up, Edvard! I'm going to help you!

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.500
Follow my orders if you want to live!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:55.790
When its eyes glow, three seconds later,
it'll shoot off a laser beam!

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.830
Focus your defensive spells on your scales and deflect it!

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.960
What?! That's a lot to take in all at--

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:04.170
What did I just tell you?!

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.670
It just deployed its left vibroblade!

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.580
Whatever you do, don't take a direct hit from that thing!

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:18.920
The blade itself is weak,
so hit it from the side to destroy it!

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:21.250
Vibro-what?! I don't understand!

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:29.040
How do you not understand?!
It's in a machine golem's basic kit!

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.330
I have never faced such a foe!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:35.670
This may be common knowledge to you,
Lord Leo, but not to me!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.130
The sword will kill you, so hit it from the side!

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.290
Understood!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:46.670
Good!

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:51.880
"Common knowledge to you, but not to me!"

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.630
That's what I wanted to hear!

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:55.460
Now!

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.080
Father, let me join you!

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:00.920
Julietta!

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:06.040
Don't get in the way! Leave this to Lord Leo and I,
lest you do yourself harm!

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:07.630
Listen to me, Father!

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:11.460
Don't be stubborn, girl! This is my fight!

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:14.250
Fall back before you get hurt!

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:16.330
Its weak point is the right side of its torso!

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:17.830
What?!

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:22.290
According to our documents, that's where its, uh...

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:28.130
Wi... Wires? Are connected to the main g-generator?

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:29.040
Strike it there!

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:31.250
Do it, Edvard!

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:34.710
Julietta's right, the right torso is where it's vulnerable!

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:36.130
Cut it down!

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.330
Father! Are you all right?!

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:08.830
I am. I couldn't have done it without your help.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.960
Julietta, Lord Leo, you have my deepest thanks.

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:16.630
Well done. He's done a good job so far!

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:19.000
All that's left is to tie things up...

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:25.710
Wait, did it just...

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:31.790
It moved!

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:35.380
I knew it! It called for backup!

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.500
Dammit, one was tough enough, but now three?!

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.750
It's no use. I'm going to have to fight them.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:45.250
My plan was going so well, too.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:48.040
But I've got no choice. I'm going to have to...

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:49.250
Fret not.

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:57.330
Shutina, prepare a defensive barrier
to protect the miners.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:58.920
Yes, Your Highness!

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:01.420
Mernes, evacuate the civilians.

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:02.250
Got it!

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:05.920
Lily, make sure there aren't any
other machine golems active in the area.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:06.960
I'm on it!

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.460
Why are they here?

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:16.580
I see. Onyx had a plan.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.790
Yep! I told you he was good!

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.210
Your Highness, where are you going?

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:22.750
He said he'd handle it,

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:27.460
but when the unexpected occurs,
even the best and brightest need help.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:32.670
And Edvard is one of my dear underlings.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:36.630
He's helped me time and time again.
If I didn't help him in his hour of need...

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:38.920
What Demon Queen would I be?!

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:41.080
Your Highness...

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.250
You see this, yes, Onyx?

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:50.830
We will handle things here.
You finish things off where you are!

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:52.460
Echidna...

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:55.170
Right, I'm on it!

00:16:56.210 --> 00:17:00.420
Stand down, you dolls of wood and metal.
Do you know who I am?

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:04.170
I stand above all demonkind as their supreme ruler:

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.330
Demon Queen Echidna!

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:09.130
Now, burn in the pits of purgatory!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.540
Inferno!

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:18.630
Thank you again, Lord Leo.

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:23.540
Wow, I didn't know the Dragon General
was such a joke in combat!

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:24.750
Lord Leo?

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:29.830
Really, how does a Great General NOT
know about laser weapons or vibroblades?

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:33.830
Everyone knows about those! Literally everyone!

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:37.500
Literally everyone?! You can't be serious!

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:41.500
Nope, I'm serious! It's the basics of the basics!

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:44.170
You must not be working hard enough!

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:48.380
How can you call yourself the Dragon General
when you can't take out a machine golem?

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:54.500
Isn't that the exact thing you told your troops
before?

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:03.250
How?! How can an entire battalion
be bested by one chimera?!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:07.790
It's impossible, sir! We've never fought one before!

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:08.500
Insolent fool!

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:12.960
When I was your age, I trained by fighting
deathmatches with these creatures daily!

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:17.210
Stop making excuses for your lack of effort!

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:18.580
But sir...

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:20.250
The backs of their legs are weak!

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.880
Slice the heels to immobilize, then smash the head!

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:28.540
Everyone knows that!
None of you are trying hard enough!

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:36.080
You're better off quitting, that's for sure!
Go back home and pick up fishing, why don'tcha!

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:37.290
Lord Leo?

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.420
I would request that you stop insulting my father.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:42.750
Julietta...

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:46.330
You musn't assume that your knowledge
is common knowledge for everyone.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:52.420
You have years of experience and familiarity,
but we have never fought a machine golem.

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:58.710
Oh, c'mon. You think you can laze around just
'cause you've never fought one before?

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:02.960
You're just making excuses for your lack of effort!

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:07.080
I am not! Anyone would have trouble
with a task they've never done before!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:11.080
How would you know how to handle
a foe you've never encountered?!

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:18.080
You mustn't assume others can do what you can.

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:24.500
You should train someone starting from the basics,
then slowly work your way up.

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:28.750
Is that not important when
you're preparing someone for battle?

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:38.210
I see. Onyx had a plan.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:58.040
G-General, sir, forgive us, but...

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:03.040
Oh, men... I'm so terribly sorry!

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:08.170
I should not have said you weren't trying hard enough!

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:12.790
Truly, the one who needed to put
in more effort was me and me alone!

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.960
I deeply apologize!

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:24.920
Don't hang your head like that, sir.

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:29.500
You're far more inspiring with your head held high.

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:35.420
He's right! We all joined the army because
we admired your strength, sir!

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:39.880
So, sir... Please, don't quit on us!

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:44.750
We'll work even harder, so please, keep training us!

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:47.330
I'm touched...

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:54.790
Very well! I have a long way to go,
but I hope you'll stand by me!

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:55.750
Yes, sir!

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:59.830
A good warrior isn't always a good boss.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:04.630
But when they've learned how to teach others,

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:06.920
a good warrior can be a truly great boss.

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:10.500
I couldn't have done this without the others.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.830
My, you can still move after that attack?

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:21.540
Then how about this!

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:23.250
Explode!

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:25.170
And a Fireball!

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:26.790
And a Plasma Cannon!

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.000
And a Hellfire!

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:30.210
And a Meteor Swarm!

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:36.710
Queen Echidna, that's enough, that's enough!

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:40.330
She needs to blow off steam. Let her be.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:44.000
Y'know, you've changed lately, Mernes!

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.080
Shush.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:05.790
Our hearts are always so frail and fragile

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:11.960
But we still face forward and continue down our long road

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:17.580
If we don't know something now, we can go learn about it

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:24.500
We might not know what's at the end of our long, continuing journey

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:30.540
Don't try to do everything yourself, lean on us sometimes

00:22:30.790 --> 00:22:34.330
Sharing your weaknesses is strength in itself

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:38.750
There's still a long way to go,
so make sure you won't regret anything

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:42.170
Dash on! The reason's simple

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:45.630
Let loose! Make your dreams reality

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:51.750
The future you're heading towards is one you shape yourself

00:22:51.750 --> 00:22:57.420
It's okay to be scared of change, you can go little by little

00:22:57.420 --> 00:23:01.580
I want to protect the things I cherish

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:04.170
(I'm so glad we found each other)

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:08.500
So I hope you hear how thankful I am for you

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:41.080
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:41.080
<b>Tokyo, 2060 A.D.</b>
